NACL (Network Access Control List) is a security layer in AWS that controls incoming and outgoing traffic for subnets inside a VPC.

why:-
-----
🛡️ Control inbound and outbound network traffic.
🚫 Allow or deny traffic based on rules.
🔒 Add an extra layer of security to subnets.
🌐 Filter traffic using IP addresses and protocol/port rules.

types:-
---------
Default NACL: By default, it allows all inbound and outbound traffic.
Custom NACL: Initially denies all traffic until you add rules to allow specific traffic.
